 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">2. The 7 cell-level checks before you pay</h2>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Run all seven at quote stage, they take under two hours</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">These checks are ordered by cost: the first four cost nothing but an email, the last three need samples. Together they expose the two fraud patterns, downgraded cells sold as Grade A, and used cells sold as new.</p>

 <table class="w-full text-sm mb-6">
 <thead class="bg-brandBlue text-white">
 <tr><th class="p-3 text-left">#</th><th class="p-3 text-left">Check</th><th class="p-3 text-left">What a passing answer looks like</th></tr>
 </thead>
 <tbody class="bg-white">
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">1</td><td class="p-3">Cell brand + exact model</td><td class="p-3">Named brand and model (e.g. LG, Samsung SDI, Panasonic), matching the quote line item</td></tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">2</td><td class="p-3">Datasheet</td><td class="p-3">Original datasheet with capacity, IR, and cycle-life curves for that model</td></tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">3</td><td class="p-3">Packaging photos with date codes</td><td class="p-3">Cell trays photographed with intact, uniform date codes, not re-wrapped film</td></tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">4</td><td class="p-3">Price sanity check</td><td class="p-3">Quote within the Grade-A band; >25% below market means the cells are not first-run</td></tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">5</td><td class="p-3">Sample discharge test</td><td class="p-3">Delivered mAh within datasheet tolerance at rated current (see section 3)</td></tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">6</td><td class="p-3">Internal resistance report</td><td class="p-3">IR values per cell within the datasheet band, measured on a batch sample</td></tr>
 <tr class="border-t border-slate-200"><td class="p-3">7</td><td class="p-3">UN38.3 report cross-check</td><td class="p-3">Report names the exact cell model and matches the cells in your samples</td></tr>
 </tbody>
 </table>

 <div class="mt-6 mb-6">
 <img src="/image/blog/power-bank/power-bank-internal-battery-cells.webp" alt="Grade-A lithium cells inside a power bank during OEM production: cell grading and traceability verification" loading="lazy" class="max-w-3xl mx-auto rounded-2xl shadow-lg w-full">
 </div>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Why checks 1-4 filter most fraud before sampling</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">A rebuilt-cell operation scales through vagueness: no model number on the quote, no datasheet, "high-quality cells" in place of a brand. Requiring all three in writing costs the supplier minutes and costs you nothing, and the suppliers who stall on checks 1-3 will not pass checks 5-7 either. Treat the price sanity check as the arithmetic backstop: cells are 35-50% of the BOM, so a quote far below the Grade-A band has to be cutting somewhere.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

